    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.29) and **Isaac Paredes** (66.30) headlining the lineup as our most efficient starts. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits significantly from a +14% platoon edge against a hittable arm, while **Isaac Paredes** continues to capitalize on favorable park factors and middle-of-the-order security. Despite facing a formidable arm, **James Wood** remains a high-floor play (63.47) given his elite xwOBA metrics and the catalytic potential of his leadoff positioning. We are keeping a close watch on **Seiya Suzuki**, whose score has dipped to a marginal 46.29 due to a difficult matchup against an elite arm (2.30 xERA), putting him in the \"start only if necessary\" bucket despite his usual reliability.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Austin Riley** on the bench with a 57.59 score. While **Austin Riley** carries strong underlying projections, he was ultimately edged out by the superior platoon and order-based efficiency scores of **Josh Naylor** and **Brice Turang**. We are also managing significant risk with **Zach McKinstry**, who occupies an OF slot with a pedestrian 43.20 score; he is essentially a \"bench to preserve\" candidate today, but we are keeping him active to chase potential SB opportunities against a high-delivery-time pitcher. Meanwhile, **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** offer moderate production profiles, but we are proceeding with caution\u2014**Trevor Story** is facing a tough pitcher, and we need **Mickey Moniak** to exploit his +14% platoon advantage to justify his start. With **Corbin Carroll** and **Jose Caballero** unavailable, we are leaning heavily on the remaining core to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity categories.",
